      h1 Pico CSS is no longer maintained @219,472,32,150
      text v2.1.1 is the final release. @219,634,32,102
    col @263,17,196,1142
      h2 Why# @263,17,196,21
      text Today, AI can generate lightweight, standalone, accessible HTML with just the CSS it needs, so a Minimal CSS Framework for Semantic HTML matters less than it used to. @263,50,196,142
      text To stay relevant, Pico CSS would need a full rewrite: plain modern CSS instead of Sass, built on features it doesn’t use today (OKLCH colors, cascade layers, Popover, anchor positioning) with fallbacks for older browsers, and a native compiler that strips unused CSS and makes customization easy. @263,204,196,244
      text That would be a different project. Pico CSS stays as it is. @263,460,196,61
      h2 What this means# @263,533,196,21
      text Nothing breaks. , the and this website stay online for the long term. @263,566,196,61
